course: dictionary
lesson: 13358
title: A word from Mandarin: hao
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hao is not an English word. It is a Mandarin Chinese word, written here in pinyin, which uses the Roman alphabet to show how Chinese words sound. When you meet a new word, use its context to work out what it means.
explain: Hǎo means «good», «well» or «fine». You will hear it often in Mandarin lessons and on the street. «Nǐ hǎo!» means «hello», because nǐ means «you».
explain: Tone matters. Hǎo has a tone that dips down and then goes up, so to an English ear it sounds a little like «how». Change the tone to hào and the meaning changes: it means a number or a date, as in «sān hào», the 3rd.
fact: Hao is not an English word. It is Mandarin Chinese, written in pinyin.
fact: Hǎo means good, well or fine.
fact: «Nǐ hǎo» means hello.
fact: Hào, said with a different tone, means a number or a date in the month, as in «sān hào» (the 3rd).
fact: The Chinese character for hǎo (好) is made of «woman» and «child» side by side.
exercise: «Nǐ hǎo!» is said to a friend in the morning. What does it mean? | *Hello | Thank you | Sorry | Goodbye
exercise: «Hǎo, let's go!» means «OK, let's go!». What does hǎo mean here? | A number | Goodbye | *OK, good | Quiet
exercise: «Today is sān hào.» In «sān hào», what does hào mean? | Good | A river | Hello | *A number or a date
test: Which English word does hao sound a little like? | *how | cat | sun | big
test: Which meaning fits hǎo most often? | a river | *good, well or fine | a train | sleepy
exam: Is hao an English word? | Yes, it means happy in English | Yes, it means fine in English only | *No, it is a Mandarin word written in pinyin | No, it is a Scots word
